\section{Appendix Z1 (parked): Localizing the concept --- ``where is Paris?'' (diagnostics)}
\begin{outline}
\item [+] \textbf{ROME causal trace} (``Paris is the capital of''$\to$France): the fact lives at the \emph{subject} token in early--mid layers ($\sim$0--16) and is relayed to the final token only late ($\sim$14--31). \texttt{ROME-PARIS.png}; \texttt{diag\_paris\_rome.ipynb}; \texttt{diag\_paris\_rome\_ha.ipynb}.
\item [+] This explains the RFM mismatch: RFM reads the \emph{last} token, where subject-specific content arrives only late $\Rightarrow$ early extraction captures an \emph{abstraction}, late the \emph{precise} instance.
\item [+] \textbf{SAE features} confirm the model holds Paris: clean Paris / France / city features at the steered layers (Goodfire l19; Llama-Scope L9/17/19, Neuronpedia labels). \texttt{diag\_paris\_sae.ipynb}, \texttt{diag\_paris\_sae\_2.ipynb}. The steering failure is extraction/geometry, not absence.
\item [?] \textbf{Tegmark spatial probe} (lat/lon linear probe): coordinates linearly decodable but under-powered at $N{=}90$ cities (median $\sim$2200\,km). \texttt{diag\_paris\_tegmark.ipynb}.
\item [+] \textbf{Where ``late'' begins}: logit-lens KL-to-output gives stage boundaries to avoid the residual-sharpening tail. \texttt{diag\_stages\_late.ipynb}.
\end{outline}

\section{Appendix Z2 (parked): Conceptual threads}
\begin{outline}
\item [?] \textbf{Abstract-early / precise-late hierarchy}: the extraction layer sets the abstraction level; the precise concept lives late (weak steering) while the strong injection point is mid (concept abstract) --- no single layer gives both.
\item [?] \textbf{Two candidate axes} (now Discussion future work): (i) abstraction-depth --- first layer that can \emph{steer} the concept; (ii) compositional basis size ($\lambda_1$/trace). Between-class confounded (moods both more composite \emph{and} earlier-steering than places); independence is a within-supersense question.
\item [--] Extraction geometry cannot proxy first-steerable-depth: rotation and alignment-to-deep proxies are concept-invariant ($\sim$17--20) and fail the steering ground truth (cross-layer orthogonality, $\cos\approx0.05$). A write property; measure by steering. \texttt{nb\_axes.ipynb}; \texttt{plots/axes\_independence.png}.
\item [?] \textbf{Superposition vs.\ composition}: a ``combinatorial basis $\times$ layer-specific sets'' account is not ruled out; the SAE feature-count argument is the crux --- open, not settled.
\item [?] \textbf{Stages of inference / lens} framing (Lad--Gurnee--Tegmark) as the principled naming of early/mid/late bands.
\item [?] \textbf{Not-all-linear} (Engels et al., arXiv:2405.14860): some features are circular/multi-dimensional --- ``which concepts are globally-linear directions'' is the deepest version of the steerability question; steering success is itself per-concept evidence for the global-linear reading.
\end{outline}
